## Proposed Changes

### 1. Frontend Dependencies
We will install the Workbox libraries to power our advanced Service Worker.
- Install `workbox-core`, `workbox-expiration`, `workbox-precaching`, `workbox-routing`, `workbox-strategies`, and `workbox-background-sync` via npm.

---

### 2. PWA Configuration & Metadata

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/public/manifest.json`
- Expand to an "extreme" manifest with `shortcuts` (e.g., direct links to "New Post", "Search"), `description`, `categories`, and `display_override`.
- Ensure high-quality icons and screenshot definitions for better install prompts.

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/public/index.html`
- Add iOS-specific meta tags (`apple-mobile-web-app-capable`, `apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style`).
- Add a theme color meta tag to match the dark/light mode setup.

---

### 3. Service Worker Implementation

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/service-worker.js`
- Create a custom Workbox-powered service worker.
- **Pre-caching**: Automatically cache all static assets compiled by CRA.
- **Runtime Caching**:
  - `NetworkFirst` strategy for our API endpoints (e.g., fetching posts).
  - `CacheFirst` for images and avatars (with expiration).
- **Background Sync**: Allow users to write posts or like posts while offline. The service worker will queue these requests and send them to the backend when the connection is restored.
- **Offline Fallback**: Serve a cached response if a network request fails and the user is entirely offline.

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/serviceWorkerRegistration.js`
- Include the standard CRA service worker registration script with added hooks to notify the React app when an update is available or when the app is installed.

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/src/index.js`
- Import and call `serviceWorkerRegistration.register()` to enable the Service Worker.

---

