- Add a custom "Install App" button or prompt that appears dynamically if the app hasn't been installed yet, making the experience feel premium.

## Verification Plan

### Automated/Local Tests
- Build the frontend (`npm run build`) and serve it locally (using `serve` or similar) to ensure the service worker registers properly, as CRA only enables SW in production builds by default.
- Use Chrome DevTools (Application tab) to verify the Service Worker, Manifest, and Background Sync queue.

### Manual Verification
- Simulate offline mode in Chrome DevTools to verify that the app still loads and displays cached posts.
- Create a post while offline and observe the Background Sync queue, then reconnect to the network to see the post automatically sync.
